## 12. ReplicationController vs ReplicaSet vs Deployment

### ReplicationController

- Older Kubernetes controller for maintaining Pod replicas.
- Uses equality-based label selectors.
- Superseded for most new workloads by ReplicaSets and Deployments.

### ReplicaSet

- Maintains a specified number of matching Pods.
- Supports label selectors, including `matchLabels`.
- Does not provide the full rollout management workflow of Deployments.

### Deployment

- Recommended for most stateless application workloads.
- Manages ReplicaSets and Pod updates.
- Supports rolling updates, rollout history, and rollbacks.

### Relationship

```text
Deployment
    |
    v
ReplicaSet
    |
    v
Pods
    |
    v
Containers
```

