## Important Notes

- Use Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, `t3.medium`, and at least 20 GB storage for this lab.
- Run Minikube as the normal `ubuntu` user when using the Docker driver.
- Containers in a Pod share the network namespace; storage is shared only when volumes are mounted appropriately.
- A standalone Pod is not automatically recreated by a ReplicaSet.
- A ReplicaSet provides replica management and self-healing, while Services normally provide stable network access.
- Use Deployments for application updates and rollbacks.
- Avoid reusing labels for unrelated workloads because selectors can match unintended Pods.
- For production environments, learn resource requests and limits, probes, Services, ConfigMaps, Secrets, persistent volumes, security, and networking.

